sequenceDiagram

actor Visitor
participant Server as server.js
participant Route as routes/auth.js + authValidation
participant Controller as controllers/auth.js
participant Models as User / Provider / ProviderApplication / AuthSession
participant DB as MongoDB
Visitor->>Server: POST /api/v1/auth/register or /auth/register-provider
activate Server
Server->>Route: Parsed JSON, registered auth path
Route->>Route: Validate and allowlist input
Route->>Controller: registerCustomer or registerProvider(req.validated)
activate Controller
Controller->>DB: startSession + withTransaction
Controller->>Models: User.create with server-assigned role
Models->>Models: User save hook hashes password
Models->>DB: Insert user in session
opt Provider registration
    Controller->>Models: Create pending Provider and application version 1
    Models->>DB: Insert linked records in same session
end
Controller->>Controller: Sign token with unique session ID
Controller->>Models: AuthSession.create in same session
Models->>DB: Insert session
Controller->>Controller: Serialize user and build result
DB-->>Controller: Commit transaction
Controller-->>Server: 201 success + data
deactivate Controller
Server-->>Visitor: JSON response
deactivate Server
Note over Controller,DB: Duplicate email or business number maps to 409, transaction failure rolls back all inserts
